 King, and then finish the hand with the Black Joker.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation:\nI hold the `♣K` and the `BlackJoker`. Based on the card counting information provided (`J: 1, 10: 1, 7: 2, 5: 1, 4: 2`), the highest card currently held by the Landlord or my Teammate is a Jack (`J`). There are no Aces, 2s, or Red Jokers remaining in the opponents\' hands. This means my `♣K` is effectively the second-highest card in the game (behind my own Black Joker) and is a guaranteed winner. There are also no potential bombs (quads) remaining as no rank has 4 unknown cards.\n\nStrategy:\n1. Play `♣K`. Since the highest opponent card is a Jack, no one can beat this.\n2. In the next turn, play `BlackJoker` as a single to finish the game.\n\nPlaying the King first is the optimal sequence to clear the hand.\n\nReason:\nThe `♣K` is the highest card in the game excluding my own `BlackJoker` (as the opponents\' highest card is a Jack). Playing the King guarantees a win of the trick, allowing me to play the Black Joker next and win the game immediately.\n\nAnswer:\n{"cards": ["♣K"]}'}
